{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization/pulls/5","id":4913848395,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVMZGKc8AAAABJONgSw","html_url":"https://github.com/trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization/pull/5","diff_url":"https://github.com/trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization/pull/5.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization/pull/5.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization/issues/5","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization/pulls/5/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization/pulls/5/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization/issues/5/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization/statuses/c14d96b0a63fceba02b2cb4469d5b3228ae46612","number":5,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"research v4.1: O14 checker independence and authorization-scope binding of C","user":{"login":"babyblueviper1","id":241826547,"node_id":"U_kgDODmn68w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/241826547?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1","html_url":"https://github.com/babyblueviper1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Implements the two findings from the v4 review, as you asked: both witnesses, each with its own mutation control, isolated from the v4 history. Base is your v4 branch (`ee1143f`), so the diff is v4.1 only.\n\nNo v4 file is edited. Everything is under `src/v4_1`, `fixtures/v4_1`, `evidence/v4_1`, `tests/v4_1`, `tools/v4_1` and `research/v4_1`. `artifacts.sha256.json` gains 17 entries, and no existing entry changes (`verify_artifacts.py`: 4649 files, no mismatches).\n\n**O14 `checker_independence`** is scenario-dependent: it is in output contract revision 3 and not in the replay, attestation or provenance contracts. The recovered judgment signer must differ from the recovered provenance signer. It is UNVERIFIABLE when either signature fails to verify.\n- Witness `negative_O14_self_judged`: a fresh lab issuance (`tools/v4_1/create_self_judged_fixture.mjs`, same pattern as v4's, keys not saved) where one key signs provenance and judgment and the policy authorizes it for both roles. v4 under the v4 output contract: VERIFIED, authorized. v4.1: REFUTED, and O14 is the only non-VERIFIED obligation.\n- Witness `omitted_O14`: the coverage alarm fires, `missing_obligations = [O14]`.\n\n**C binding.** C carries `binding = {scenario, claim_type, contract_sha256}`. Per your note, `contract_sha256` is recomputed in `evaluate()` from the exact contract object, never copied from the claim or a result. A claim that brings its own `contract_sha256` is refused as an unconsumed field.\n- Consumption is observed: the claim is wrapped, and the reads made by each required obligation are recorded. Fields no required obligation read are listed in `unconsumed_claim_fields` and refuse C. If a required check ended UNVERIFIABLE, its reads are unknown and the result is UNVERIFIABLE instead.\n- Witness `unconsumed_output_under_replay` (the negative_O13 claim under replay): v4 gives VERIFIED, authorized. v4.1 gives REFUTED, `[outputHash]`.\n- Your negative control is `admit(result, contract, claim_type)` on the consumer side, which recomputes the digest from the contract the consumer holds:\n  - `reused_under_other_contract`: the self-judged result, authorized under the v4 output contract, is presented to a consumer holding revision 3. Same scenario name and same claim type, so only the digest separates them. Not admitted.\n  - `reused_under_other_claim_type`: `positive_replay`'s result with the output claim type requested. Not admitted.\n  - Controls: each positive is admitted under its own contract. A result whose `binding.claim_type` was edited is still refused.\n\n**Results**\n- 58 rows (54 v4 rows carried + 4 new) and 4 reuse cases: all fixed oracles hold.\n- C false authorizations 0/54, positives 4/4, false admissions 0.\n- 13 tests, normal and `-O`.\n- 6 physical mutants, run before / mutant / restored with a positive control, in normal and `-O`: 6/6 killed, 0 survived, 0 crashed, bytes restored. The six: O14 catalog deletion, O14 presence, O14 verification, the `claim_fields` guard, the `admit` digest recompute, the `admit` claim-type check.\n\nDeclared adjustments to the carried v4 rows:\n- the output contract is revision 3 (+O14);\n- the narrow-profile positives present only the claim fields their contract reads (`PROFILE_FIELDS`);\n- `omitted_O01` expects B = UNVERIFIABLE, because O14 depends on O01.\n\nLimits are in `research/v4_1/README.md`:\n- O14 compares keys, not key holders.\n- Consumption means reads by the current predicates.\n- The digest is over the parsed contract, not the file bytes.\n\nReproduce with Python 3.12, Node 22.15.0 and `tools/v3/prepare.py --online`:\n```sh\npython -B tools/v4_1/run.py\npython -B -m unittest -v tests.v4_1.test_v4_1\npython -B tools/v4_1/mutations.py --out build/v4_1/mutations\n```\nOutputs from our run are in `evidence/v4_1/validation`. Keep it as a draft, same as #4.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-18T23:42:59Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T21:16:14Z","closed_at":"2026-10-21T21:16:14Z","merged_at":"2026-10-21T21:16:13Z","merge_commit_sha":"ed298cc6a3d0215343be04b490b8f6343b05c098","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"babyblueviper1:research/v4.1-checker-independence-binding","ref":"research/v4.1-checker-independence-binding","repo":{"id":1424918510,"node_id":"R_kgDOVO6H7g","name":"verifiable-ai-guarantee-composition","full_name":"babyblueviper1/verifiable-ai-guarantee-composition","owner":{"login":"babyblueviper1","id":241826547,"node_id":"U_kgDODmn68w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/241826547?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1","html_url":"https://github.com/babyblueviper1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babyblueviper1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":true,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Experimental research on guarantee preservation across verifiable AI inference, attestations, exec